From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: Input: Keep the size of the button count's snprintf() from going negative

input_print_modalias() prints the modalias in two passes, and its first pass
calls input_print_modalias_parts(NULL, 0, 0, id) to measure the length. Every
snprintf() of that function is therefore given max(size - len, 0), since len
grows past size. The line "Input: Add info about EV_BTN" added for the button
count passes size - len itself: in the measuring pass that is a negative int,
which becomes a size_t above INT_MAX, so vsnprintf() warns and returns 0:

  WARNING: lib/vsprintf.c:2876 at vsnprintf+0x...
   snprintf
   input_print_modalias_parts
   input_print_modalias
   input_dev_uevent

once per boot, at the first input device's uevent, and the kernel is tainted
(W). The measured length also comes out short by the "tN" part, so the trimming
of key data that the second pass does for a small buffer works from a length
that is too small. Use max(size - len, 0), as the lines around it do.

[ORDER 664: not part of Tomasz Pakuła's posted series; found on two installed machines on 2026-11-17 and 18
(kernel 7.3.4-stereo3d18). A follow-up of 0002-Add-info-about-EV-BTN.patch of this group, kept as a patch of its own
so the group's first six stay the text as posted.
Description: the modalias measuring pass no longer warns in vsnprintf() and counts the button count's characters
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no (the facts for a note to the series' author are prepared, row 664)
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
Proof: the function's own text from the patched tree, built against a shim with the kernel's size check: before, one
warning and a measured length 2 short for a 1-digit count; after, no warning and the measured length equal to the
printed one (sparky-os/tests/kernel-ev-btn-modalias). The next kernel build must show no "WARNING: lib/vsprintf.c" in
the journal of a start and /proc/sys/kernel/tainted without bit 9 (512).
Drop it when the author's next version of the series carries the same change.]
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2 via Claude Code
---
 drivers/input/input.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/input.c b/drivers/input/input.c
--- a/drivers/input/input.c
+++ b/drivers/input/input.c
@@ -1433,7 +1433,7 @@
 				'f', id->ffbit, 0, FF_MAX);
 	len += input_print_modalias_bits(buf + len, size - len,
 				'w', id->swbit, 0, SW_MAX);
-	len += snprintf(buf + len, size - len, "t%u", id->button_count);
+	len += snprintf(buf + len, max(size - len, 0), "t%u", id->button_count);
 
 	return len;
 }
